@startuml menu_generation
title MenuOrchestrator.generate_menu() — main outcomes
actor User
participant CLI
participant MenuOrchestrator as App
participant SystemExclusions as System
participant TimeSlotGenerator as Slots
participant MealBlockGenerator as Blocks
participant AvailableRecipeList as Available
participant RecipeRepository as Recipes
participant RecipeExclusions as Exclusions
participant MenuPlanner as Planner
participant Menu

User -> CLI : request a menu
CLI -> App : generate_menu()
App -> System : clear()

alt generation, planning, and exclusion population succeed
  App -> Slots : generate_timeslots(14)
  Slots --> App : 14 TimeSlot
  App -> Blocks : generate_mealblocks(14)
  Blocks -> Available : generate_available_recipe_list()
  Available -> Recipes : list_recipes()
  Recipes --> Available : recipes
  loop for each recipe
    Available -> Exclusions : is_excluded(recipe.id)
    Exclusions --> Available : bool
  end
  Available --> Blocks : non-excluded recipes
  Blocks --> App : MealBlock[]
  App -> Planner : plan(timeslots, mealblocks)
  Planner --> App : Menu (stable)
  App -> System : clear()
  App -> Menu : get_unique_mealblocks()
  Menu --> App : unique MealBlock[]
  loop for each unique MealBlock
    App -> System : add_system_exclusion(block.recipe_snapshot.id)
  end
  App --> CLI : MenuOrchestratorResult(success=True, menu=Menu)
else ValueError before exclusion synchronization
  note right of App
    A functional failure can arise while generating slots,
    selecting blocks, or planning; it is not planner-specific.
  end note
  App --> CLI : MenuOrchestratorResult(success=False, menu=None)
else unexpected exception before exclusion synchronization
  note right of App
    Repository access or another operation may fail.
  end note
  App --> CLI : MenuOrchestratorResult(success=False, menu=None)
end
CLI --> User : display result

note right of Blocks
Selection is random. Used recipe IDs are tracked in a
local set only during generate_mealblocks(); the set is
discarded when that call ends. It is not SystemExclusions.
end note

note left of System
The depicted failure paths leave this set empty after
the initial clear(). Successful planning is followed by
population from the final Menu's unique blocks.
An exception during population could leave a partial set;
that edge case is outside the failure paths drawn here.
end note

@enduml
